---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from "../site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy · AutoSEO.run"
  description="How AutoSEO.run handles information you submit on this site and during early access."
>
  <div class="container">
    <Header />
    <main id="main" class="privacy-copy">
      <a class="button button--secondary button--small back-link" href="/">Back</a>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p><strong>Last updated: August 26, 2026</strong></p>
      <p>
        This policy covers autoseo.run and the hosted AutoSEO product we operate. It is written for operators
        applying for early access, not for a consumer app store listing.
      </p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Application details you submit: name, work email, company or desk, site, role, volume, current setup, and the note you write.</li>
        <li>Account and workspace data if we later grant access: messages, briefs, campaign status, and files you put on the desk.</li>
        <li>Technical logs needed to run and secure the service: IP address, user agent, timestamps, and diagnostics.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To decide whether early access is a fit, and to schedule a call if you asked for one.</li>
        <li>To operate the product if you are accepted.</li>
        <li>To reply to support and meet legal obligations.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Processors</h2>
      <p>
        Applications may be stored in our analytics and email tools. Work on the desk may be sent to model,
        browser, and mail providers only as needed to do the job you requested. We do not sell applicant or
        customer data.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We keep applications long enough to review them and contact you. Hosted workspace data stays while the
        account is active. Ask us to delete an application or an account at the address below.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        AutoSEO.run<br />
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
      </p>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
